<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    brk trap as a no-return point (`option callothernoreturn on|off`).

    Issue: an AArch64 `brk` lifts to `pc = SoftwareBreakpoint(imm, next); goto [pc];`.
    The flow cannot resolve that jump, so it fell back to an ordinary call with no
    no-return mark: `(*SoftwareBreakpoint(0xc471,..))() // jump-as-call`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow-classification, `p2_lift` jump-table recovery
    (`stage_jump_table`): a jump whose target a CALLOTHER forms is `fail_callother`,
    the C++ mode the flow never reached. The trap is named by its user-op
    (`SoftwareBreakpoint`), so no other CALLOTHER jump changes.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes load the
    `macho_arm64e_auth` fixture (see the fixtures README), whose `_tail_auth` holds
    the `brk #0xc471` trap. Both passes set `ptrauthtrap off` so the trap block is
    kept in the output.

    Pass 1 (`option callothernoreturn off`) reproduces the BUG: the trap prints as a
    jump-as-call. Pass 2 (the shipped default, `callothernoreturn on`) is the FIX:
    the trap is marked no-return.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_arm64e_auth</com>
  <com>option ptrauthtrap off</com>
  <com>option callothernoreturn off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function _tail_auth</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_arm64e_auth</com>
  <com>option ptrauthtrap off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function _tail_auth</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="BRKNORETURN #1: off: the trap is a call that falls back to jump-as-call" min="1" max="1">SoftwareBreakpoint\(0xc471,0x100000444\)\)\(\); // jump-as-call</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="BRKNORETURN #2: on: the trap is marked no-return" min="1" max="1">SoftwareBreakpoint\(0xc471,0x100000444\)\)\(\); // no-return</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="BRKNORETURN #3: the tail call survives in both passes" min="2" max="2">_helper2\(\); // tail-call</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
